# love_ui_rect() outside a window/panel/popup must be a script error, not an
# abort. microui's draw commands read the top of its clip stack through
# expect(), which calls abort(), and nothing but a container pushes onto it --
# so the editor's cursor label used to take the whole process down the moment
# it drew. The runner also insists an xfail dies with a plain exit code rather
# than a signal, which is the half of this that regressed.

fn love_load() {
    love_ui_begin();
    love_ui_rect(10, 10, 40, 20, 255, 0, 0, 255);
    love_ui_end();
    println("CLOVE_TEST_OK");
    love_event_quit();
}

fn main() {}
